  "function": {
    "uniprot_function": "Key downstream component of the canonical Wnt signaling pathway. In the absence of Wnt, forms a complex with AXIN1, AXIN2, APC, CSNK1A1 and GSK3B that promotes phosphorylation on N-terminal Ser and Thr residues and ubiquitination of CTNNB1 via BTRC and its subsequent degradation by the proteasome. In the presence of Wnt ligand, CTNNB1 is not ubiquitinated and accumulates in the nucleus, where it acts as a coactivator for transcription factors of the TCF/LEF family, leading to activation of Wnt responsive genes. Involved in the regulation of cell adhesion, as component of an E-cadherin:catenin adhesion complex. Acts as a negative regulator of centrosome cohesion. Involved in the CDK2/CCND1-mediated phosphorylation of APC and the regulation of APC function in cell cycle. Sustains the mitotic checkpoint by inhibition of FZR1/CDH1 and its ubiquitin ligase activity. Required for the cleavage of RBPJ during neuronal differentiation.",
    "catalytic_activity": "Not applicable (non-enzymatic structural and regulatory protein)",
    "subcellular_location": [
      "Cytoplasm",
      "Nucleus (upon Wnt stimulation)",
      "Cell membrane (adherens junction)",
      "Centrosome (during mitosis)"
    ],
    "tissue_specificity": "Expressed in many tissues with particularly high levels in colon epithelium, hair follicles, and throughout the developing embryo. Low tissue specificity indicates broad expression pattern.",
